From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haoze <90812991+HaozeG@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:21:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [shvla] FlooNoC reductions start from the identity; fp16
 subnormal conversion

Router::collective_generate forks a reduction (collective types 2..7) into kid requests and
process_collective_operations folds each kid's data into the parent's. The parent's data was never
set to the identity: at the source router it is the iDMA read buffer (uninitialised heap), at a
forking kid a copy of it. Every forking router therefore added that buffer once. Seen as
FlatAttention with flatten_scale_x > 1: every output element off by the same constant,
(sx - 1) x 0xAAAA (-0.052) under MALLOC_PERTURB_=85; sx = 1 configurations were correct.
The parent buffer is now filled with 0 (add, max uint16), -32768 (max int16) or -inf (max fp16)
before its kids are generated.

float_to_fp16 shifted fp16 subnormals by (1 - e) instead of (14 - e), spilling 13 bits into the
exponent and sign; fp16_to_float read fp16 subnormals as float denormals (about 0). Both fixed.
Data only; no timing change. Carried in soft_hier/gvsoc_pulp.patch and in the patched pulp working
tree (pulp/pulp/floonoc/floonoc.cpp, floonoc_router.cpp).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
